You are working in the GitHub repository `Kozea/Radicale`. Write a patch (unified diff) that resolves the following issue. The patch must be correct and safe to merge.

<issue>
Storage hook only adds path to item in PUT
The [storage] hook path attribute should have the full path to the item, according to the [documentation](https://radicale.org/v3.html#hook).
However, in the cases DELETE, MKCOL, MKCALENDAR, MOVE, and PROPPATCH, this path points to `collections/collection-root`, instead of `collections/collection-root/user/collection/item.ics`

This should be implemented for DELETE, MKCOL, MKCALENDAR, MOVE, and PROPPATCH.

This issue seems to be that many calls to `StoragePartLock.acquire_lock()` don't include the path.
</issue>

